# process.nextTick(() => {})
# The table has a row for `new process.nextTick(..)`, which answers an object that it says nothing of. Nobody constructs here, so that row makes nothing. If every row of a built-in in use counted, objects of any class might exist,
# native code would find `constructor` on the prototype object of each class, and what hangs on the objects of AbortController, the printer of warnings, would be in a program of one line.
# The queue of ticks is there: the library makes the value of process.nextTick.
